==> [5/5] Run constraint tests (5 expected PASS)
================================================================
 Constraint tests — each block is expected to raise an error.
================================================================

[TEST 1] Duplicate student email — should FAIL with unique_violation
psql:constraint_tests.sql:33: NOTICE:  TEST 1 PASS: duplicate email rejected — duplicate key value violates unique constraint "students_email_key"
DO

[TEST 2] Payment in wrong currency — should FAIL with foreign_key_violation
psql:constraint_tests.sql:60: NOTICE:  TEST 2 PASS: wrong-currency payment rejected — insert or update on table "payments" violates foreign key constraint "fk_pay_invoice_currency"
DO

[TEST 3] In-person session with no school — should FAIL with check_violation
psql:constraint_tests.sql:78: NOTICE:  TEST 3 PASS: in-person session without school rejected — new row for relation "sessions" violates check constraint "chk_inperson_school"
DO

[TEST 4] Session capacity exceeded — should FAIL (trigger exception)
psql:constraint_tests.sql:125: NOTICE:  TEST 4 control: first 8 bookings succeeded
psql:constraint_tests.sql:125: NOTICE:  TEST 4 PASS: capacity exceeded rejected - Session 11257 is full (capacity=8, already booked=8). Booking rejected.
DO

[TEST 5] Student not enrolled in course — should FAIL (trigger exception)
psql:constraint_tests.sql:163: NOTICE:  TEST 5 PASS: not-enrolled booking rejected — Student 1118 is not actively enrolled in course 1 (session 11258). Booking rejected.
DO

================================================================
 End of constraint tests — all 5 should report PASS above.
